[[File:Wolverhampton UK local election 2022 map.svg|thumb|Results of the 2022 City of Wolverhampton Council election]]
The '''2022 City of Wolverhampton Council election''' took place on 5 May 2022 to elect members of [[City of Wolverhampton Council]]. This was on the same day as [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections]]. 20 of the 60 seats were up for election.<ref>{{cite web |title=Election timetable in England |url=https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/election-timetable-in-england/election-timetable-in-england#metropolitan-districts |website=GOV.UK |access-date=9 April 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

==Background==
Since its first election in [[1973 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1973]], Wolverhampton Council has been a [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] council, aside from a brief period from to [[1978 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1978]] to [[1979 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1979]] when the party was overtaken by the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservatives]]. Labour has controlled the council for its entire existence apart from brief periods of [[no overall control]] (1978 to [[1980 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1980]], [[1987 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1987]] to [[1988 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1988]], [[1992 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1992]] to [[1994 Wolverhampton Metropolitan Borough Council election|1994]], and [[2008 Wolverhampton City Council election|2008]] to [[2011 Wolverhampton City Council election|2011]]).<ref>{{cite web |title=Wolverhampton City Council Election Results 1973-2012 |url=http://www.electionscentre.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/Wolverhampton-1973-2012.pdf |website=Elections Centre |access-date=14 April 2022}}</ref> In the [[2021 Wolverhampton City Council election|2021 election]], Labour lost 5 seats with 47.2% of the vote, and the Conservatives gained 5 seats with 43.0%.

The seats up for election this year were last elected in [[2018 City of Wolverhampton Council election|2018]]. In that election, Labour gained 2 seats with 58.04% of the vote, the Conservatives lost 1 with 33.69%, and [[UK Independence Party|UKIP]] lost representation on the council with 0.93%.<ref>{{cite web |title=Election results by party, 3 May 2018 |url=https://wolverhampton.moderngov.co.uk/mgElectionResults.aspx?ID=13&RPID=3534596 |website=Wolverhampton.gov |access-date=14 April 2022 |language=en-gb |date=3 May 2018}}</ref>

